# CH08 — Traitor's Edge. Whitebone Redoubt, Oni, the Ivory Adjudicator.

@scene D07_SABLE_GATE once
say sable | Stop. I'm alone and I'm not armed for you. Crimson Oni, binding officer. Until this morning.
say dain | You wrote the warrants.
say sable | I wrote the seals. The warrants were written above me. That distinction won't matter to you and it shouldn't.
say sable | The prisoners inside are bound by my seals. I can walk you to them. In return, safe conduct out of the Basin.
say oriel | No. We will not trade one set of prisoners for another bargain. We go in to free them properly.
say sable | Properly?
say oriel | Each seal is keyed to a warrant number. Replace it with a key the person inside actually gives us. Their name. Their consent.
say sable | ...That's slower.
say oriel | Yes.
say sable | Fine. I'll show you the Names Hall. You won't like how little is written there.
say narr | (The Barracks lead north to the Names Hall and east to the Binding Cells. Read each seal; ask each prisoner.)
objective oriel | Record each prisoner's own consent key: read their seal in the Names Hall, ask them in the Binding Cells.
@end

@scene D07_SEAL1
if flag:d07_name1 read
set d07_name1
say narr | Seal 4471. A warrant number, a date, and in a smaller hand at the edge: 'Hallen - weaver.'
end
label read
say narr | Seal 4471: Hallen, weaver.
@end

@scene D07_SEAL2
if flag:d07_name2 read
set d07_name2
say narr | Seal 4472. No name at all. Scratched into the stone beneath it: 'Ysa'.
end
label read
say narr | Seal 4472: Ysa.
@end

@scene D07_SEAL3
if flag:d07_name3 read
set d07_name3
say narr | Seal 4473. 'Dragonborn, unit of the Cinder line.' Beside it, in chalk, a child's letters: 'CORVIN'.
end
label read
say narr | Seal 4473: Corvin.
@end

@scene D07_PRISONER1
if flag:d07_open1 free
if flag:d07_consent1 given
say survivor | Hallen. I weave. Wove. Are you here to move me to another cell?
say oriel | We're here to ask whether you want to leave. If you do, your name opens the lock.
say survivor | ...Yes. Hallen. I want to leave.
set d07_consent1
end
label given
say survivor | Hallen. I said yes. I'll keep saying it.
end
label free
say survivor | Thank you is too small. I'll find a bigger word later.
@end

@scene D07_PRISONER2
if flag:d07_open2 free
if flag:d07_consent2 given
say survivor | Don't open it yet. Not until you've asked the others. I won't be first out and leave them.
say oriel | We'll ask each of them. What is your name?
say survivor | Ysa. And yes. After them, or with them. Not before.
set d07_consent2
end
label given
say survivor | Ysa. Yes - with the others.
end
label free
say survivor | Together. Good.
@end

@scene D07_PRISONER3
if flag:d07_open3 free
if flag:d07_consent3 given
say survivor | They call me by the seal number. I've started calling myself by it too. That's the worst part.
say dain | The Names Hall says Corvin.
say survivor | Someone wrote that? ...Corvin. Yes. That's me. Let me out.
set d07_consent3
end
label given
say survivor | Corvin. Say it again when you open it.
end
label free
say survivor | Corvin. Out loud. I'll get used to it.
@end

@scene D07_LOCK1
call D07_LOCK_TEMPLATE_1
@end

@scene D07_LOCK_TEMPLATE_1
if flag:d07_open1 done
if !flag:d07_name1 noname
if !flag:d07_consent1 noconsent
sfx FX024
set d07_open1
say narr | The binding sigil dims. In its place, a new key glows with a single word: HALLEN. The door opens.
call D07_SABLE_TEACH
end
label noname
say narr | The seal is keyed to a warrant number. Read the name in the Names Hall first.
end
label noconsent
say narr | You have the name, but not the person's answer. Ask the one inside.
end
label done
say narr | The cell is open.
@end

@scene D07_LOCK2
if flag:d07_open2 done
if !flag:d07_name2 noname
if !flag:d07_consent2 noconsent
if !flag:d07_open1 wait
sfx FX024
set d07_open2
say narr | YSA. The second door opens, after the first, as she asked.
end
label wait
say narr | Ysa asked to leave with the others, not before them.
end
label noname
say narr | The seal is keyed to a warrant number. Read the name in the Names Hall first.
end
label noconsent
say narr | You have the name, but not the person's answer. Ask the one inside.
end
label done
say narr | The cell is open.
@end

@scene D07_LOCK3
if flag:d07_open3 done
if !flag:d07_name3 noname
if !flag:d07_consent3 noconsent
sfx FX024
set d07_open3
say narr | CORVIN. The last sigil gives way.
end
label noname
say narr | The seal is keyed to a warrant number. Read the name in the Names Hall first.
end
label noconsent
say narr | You have the name, but not the person's answer. Ask the one inside.
end
label done
say narr | The cell is open.
@end

@scene D07_SABLE_TEACH once
say sable | That's my seal design you just replaced. I built it so no one could change the key without the warrant office.
say sable | You did it with a name and a question.
say sable | If I'm going to be useful: my blade takes an infusion - fire, ice or storm - and my runes strip what enemies are wearing. One infusion at a time.
join C07
say narr | Oni's Runes infuse his blade and unseal enemy protections. Formation lets you choose your active five at safe points.
objective sable | Free all three prisoners, then face whatever holds the Tribunal Ring.
@end

@scene D07_ADJUDICATOR once
music silence
say narr | The Tribunal Ring. An ivory figure holds a warrant bearing Raven's description - and a ward seal meant for a dragonborn.
say "Adjudicator" | HOST LOCATED. TRANSFER OF WARD TO SUBJECT RAVEN. AUTHORISED BY OFFICER ONI.
say dain | Oni.
say sable | I authorised a transfer template. Years ago. I didn't know it would ever be you.
say "Adjudicator" | OFFICER ONI. APPLY YOUR SEAL. COMPLETE THE TRANSFER.
say narr | Oni raises his officer's seal. For a moment it could go either way. Then he breaks it across his knee.
say sable | Transfer refused.
say oriel | Its sigil shows whether the next seal targets skills or strength. Alternate commands; Attack and Defend are never both locked.
battle B07 noflee
set b07_done
music M020
say narr | The Adjudicator's ivory cracks into plain chalk. The ward template it carried dissolves with it.
xp 320
@end

@scene CH08_SNOW once
say narr | The Snow Exit. The freed prisoners walk out first, blinking in the white.
say survivor | You broke your seal instead of using it.
say sable | Yes.
say survivor | That was useful. It's not forgiveness.
say sable | I know.
say survivor | Nacre keeps a hearing house. Send your testimony there. Your name, in your own hand.
say sable | I will. And I'll come back to answer it. When this is done - whatever this is.
say dain | You'll travel with us until then.
say sable | Under that understanding. Yes.
chapter CH08
say rook | Now the Memory Vault. North of Nacre. Everything the relays remember is kept there.
objective rook | Go to Nacre (east of Whitebone), then north to the Memory Vault.
discover L_T06
discover L_D08
level_floor 17
@end
